<div class="faq-sec bg-graphite">
  <div class="faq-block mx-a max-w-4xl px-16 md:px-36">
    <h2 class="faq-title c-graphite-25 font-lufga m-0 mb-48 p-0 text-center">
      Frequently asked questions
    </h2>

    <div class="faq-list flex flex-column">
      
        




<details class="faq-item c-graphite-25" >
  <summary class="faq-row flex align-center justify-between gap-24 py-32 cursor-pointer">
    <span class="faq-question c-graphite-25 font-lufga fs-24 fw-n">
      Why should I pay for search?
    </span>
    <svg class="faq-icon c-graphite-25"
      viewBox="0 0 24 24"
      fill="none"
      xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
      width="28"
      height="28"
      aria-hidden="true">
      <path d="M6 9L12 15L18 9"
        stroke="currentColor"
        stroke-width="1.5"
        stroke-linecap="round"
        stroke-linejoin="round" />
    </svg>
  </summary>

  <div class="faq-answer c-graphite-200 fs-base m-0 pb-32">
    You're already paying with your time and attention to advertisers who manipulate your search results, waste your time, and exploit your privacy. Pay with your wallet instead of your life, and get pure, powerful search that works for you - not advertisers. <a href='https://blog.kagi.com/the-many-benefits-of-paying-for-search'>Read more.</a>
  </div>
</details>





<details class="faq-item c-graphite-25" >
  <summary class="faq-row flex align-center justify-between gap-24 py-32 cursor-pointer">
    <span class="faq-question c-graphite-25 font-lufga fs-24 fw-n">
      What are the limitations of the Trial plan?
    </span>
    <svg class="faq-icon c-graphite-25"
      viewBox="0 0 24 24"
      fill="none"
      xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
      width="28"
      height="28"
      aria-hidden="true">
      <path d="M6 9L12 15L18 9"
        stroke="currentColor"
        stroke-width="1.5"
        stroke-linecap="round"
        stroke-linejoin="round" />
    </svg>
  </summary>

  <div class="faq-answer c-graphite-200 fs-base m-0 pb-32">
    The trial plan has a limit of 100 searches and 100 interactions with Kagi Assistant. You will still be able to try all of Kagi's features.
  </div>
</details>





<details class="faq-item c-graphite-25" >
  <summary class="faq-row flex align-center justify-between gap-24 py-32 cursor-pointer">
    <span class="faq-question c-graphite-25 font-lufga fs-24 fw-n">
      Terms of Kagi Assistant
    </span>
    <svg class="faq-icon c-graphite-25"
      viewBox="0 0 24 24"
      fill="none"
      xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
      width="28"
      height="28"
      aria-hidden="true">
      <path d="M6 9L12 15L18 9"
        stroke="currentColor"
        stroke-width="1.5"
        stroke-linecap="round"
        stroke-linejoin="round" />
    </svg>
  </summary>

  <div class="faq-answer c-graphite-200 fs-base m-0 pb-32">
    Plans offering access to Kagi Assistant are subject to our <a href='https://help.kagi.com/kagi/ai/assistant.html#fair-use-policy'>Fair Use Policy</a> to ensure sustainable access for everyone. You can make additional payments to resume access if you encounter our limits.
  </div>
</details>





<details class="faq-item c-graphite-25" >
  <summary class="faq-row flex align-center justify-between gap-24 py-32 cursor-pointer">
    <span class="faq-question c-graphite-25 font-lufga fs-24 fw-n">
      What happens if I don’t use my plan for a month?
    </span>
    <svg class="faq-icon c-graphite-25"
      viewBox="0 0 24 24"
      fill="none"
      xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
      width="28"
      height="28"
      aria-hidden="true">
      <path d="M6 9L12 15L18 9"
        stroke="currentColor"
        stroke-width="1.5"
        stroke-linecap="round"
        stroke-linejoin="round" />
    </svg>
  </summary>

  <div class="faq-answer c-graphite-200 fs-base m-0 pb-32">
    In months where you don't utilize your plan, we will automatically apply a full credit to your account. This credit will be applied to your next billing cycle, effectively covering your subsequent month's subscription at no additional cost.
  </div>
</details>





<details class="faq-item c-graphite-25" >
  <summary class="faq-row flex align-center justify-between gap-24 py-32 cursor-pointer">
    <span class="faq-question c-graphite-25 font-lufga fs-24 fw-n">
      Can I upgrade or downgrade at any time?
    </span>
    <svg class="faq-icon c-graphite-25"
      viewBox="0 0 24 24"
      fill="none"
      xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
      width="28"
      height="28"
      aria-hidden="true">
      <path d="M6 9L12 15L18 9"
        stroke="currentColor"
        stroke-width="1.5"
        stroke-linecap="round"
        stroke-linejoin="round" />
    </svg>
  </summary>

  <div class="faq-answer c-graphite-200 fs-base m-0 pb-32">
    Yes, you can upgrade or downgrade whenever suits you and your unused balance will be pro-rated and applied to your new plan.
  </div>
</details>





<details class="faq-item c-graphite-25" >
  <summary class="faq-row flex align-center justify-between gap-24 py-32 cursor-pointer">
    <span class="faq-question c-graphite-25 font-lufga fs-24 fw-n">
      Can I pay with PayPal or OpenNode/Bitcoin?
    </span>
    <svg class="faq-icon c-graphite-25"
      viewBox="0 0 24 24"
      fill="none"
      xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
      width="28"
      height="28"
      aria-hidden="true">
      <path d="M6 9L12 15L18 9"
        stroke="currentColor"
        stroke-width="1.5"
        stroke-linecap="round"
        stroke-linejoin="round" />
    </svg>
  </summary>

  <div class="faq-answer c-graphite-200 fs-base m-0 pb-32">
    Kagi supports alternative payment methods like PayPal or OpenNode, which is a Bitcoin payment processor. These payment methods will not create a subscription and can be used to top off your account with credits, which will then be used to fund your Kagi membership.
  </div>
</details>





<details class="faq-item c-graphite-25" >
  <summary class="faq-row flex align-center justify-between gap-24 py-32 cursor-pointer">
    <span class="faq-question c-graphite-25 font-lufga fs-24 fw-n">
      Tell me more!
    </span>
    <svg class="faq-icon c-graphite-25"
      viewBox="0 0 24 24"
      fill="none"
      xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
      width="28"
      height="28"
      aria-hidden="true">
      <path d="M6 9L12 15L18 9"
        stroke="currentColor"
        stroke-width="1.5"
        stroke-linecap="round"
        stroke-linejoin="round" />
    </svg>
  </summary>

  <div class="faq-answer c-graphite-200 fs-base m-0 pb-32">
    <p>See our <a href='https://help.kagi.com/kagi/faq/faq.html'>FAQ</a> or feel free to reach out at <a href='mailto:support@kagi.com'>support@kagi.com</a>.</p>
  </div>
</details>


      
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

